# Why every setting, env var, header and command this gateway uses is here.
#
# The rule, from the published methodology: a setting may appear only if it is needed to boot the
# process at all, to point an upstream at the test mock instead of a real provider, to expose an
# ingress path the matrix exercises, or to bind the port and cores the rig requires. One claim per
# line: <pattern> <boot|upstream|ingress|bind>. Anything unclaimed is a lint failure, and a claim
# that matches nothing is a stale claim and also a failure.
#
# Migrated from GW_CONFIG_WHY in gateway.sh, which is dead code the lint was still reading.
model_list     boot      # the proxy serves nothing without one
model_name     ingress   # the client-facing name each matrix column asks for
litellm_params boot
model          upstream  # the provider prefix selects the upstream dialect
api_base       upstream  # -> the mock
api_key        boot      # a provider entry with no key is rejected (dummy; the mock ignores it)
aws_bedrock_runtime_endpoint upstream  # bedrock's own base-URL override -> the mock
aws_access_key_id     boot   # the SigV4 signer needs some credential; the mock ignores the signature
aws_secret_access_key boot
aws_region_name       boot
master_key           boot   # v1.108.3 refuses an unset or known-default master key; the rig uses its declared nonempty mock credential without weakening the shipped check

use_chat_completions_api upstream # Only the Chat model alias declares its upstream operation. litellm/responses/main.py documents this switch for Responses-to-Chat bridging; the separate Responses alias retains native Responses. This chooses the matrix wire, without changing request contents, caches, retries, concurrency or timeouts.

The global use_chat_completions_url_for_anthropic_messages override is deliberately absent. With the Chat upstream already selected per model, the default Messages bridge reaches the correct wire but returns empty content. Switching the global bridge would hide that released failure. Keep the supported cell enabled and retain the invalid response as evidence.

COHERE_API_BASE upstream # Native /cohere/v2/chat passthrough has a separate documented base override; redirect it to the same mock.
COHERE_API_KEY boot # Dummy upstream credential for the native passthrough route.
cell_paths ingress # Native Cohere and Bedrock passthrough require /cohere and /bedrock prefixes. Bedrock resolves its existing configured model alias; Cohere uses the native command-r model id.
